## The 7 Picks — Detailed Breakdown

### Pick 1 — Classic White Gold Entry: $4,530

**Setting:** [Tapered Grooved Solitaire in 14K White Gold — $1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-tapered-grooved-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147386?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Stone:** [GIA G-VS1 1ct Excellent Cut — $3,530](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28823788?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Total: $4,530**

This is the correct answer for most men. The tapered grooved solitaire has a single groove running the band width. It is not flashy. It does not compete with the stone. The stone is 6.5mm, GIA G-VS1 Excellent cut. Eye-clean, colorless, certified.

The VS1 clarity is one tier above VS2. At 1ct, VS1 is 99% eye-clean. The $3,530 price is at the lower end of the G-VS1 range in certified inventory. This is not a discounted stone — it is correctly priced.

**Verdict:** Buy this ring if you want a first diamond ring that holds its value, looks correct, and costs less than $5,000. This is what $4,530 is worth in men's diamond rings. See [Men's 1 Carat Diamond Ring](/mens-1-carat-diamond-ring) for a full breakdown of grade and setting options at this price.

---

### Pick 2 — Yellow Gold with Colorless Stone: $4,540

**Setting:** [Tapered Grooved Solitaire in 14K Yellow Gold — $1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-tapered-grooved-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-147387?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Stone:** [GIA E-VS2 1ct Excellent Cut — $3,540](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27878143?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Total: $4,540**

Yellow gold is the right choice for a specific buyer. If you wear [yellow gold](/mens-yellow-gold-diamond-ring) elsewhere — a watch, a chain, a bracelet — this metal is the right call. It does not clash. It reads as intentional.

The stone here is E-VS2. E is one step below D — the second colorless grade. In yellow gold, colorless grades read differently than in [white gold](/mens-white-gold-diamond-ring). The warm metal slightly amplifies any residual warmth in the stone. E color eliminates that variable. The VS2 clarity is correct for 1ct. The $3,540 price on the E-VS2 is competitive — E color at 1ct typically runs $3,500–$3,800.

**Verdict:** Buy this ring if yellow gold is your metal. The E color is worth the small premium over G in yellow gold — it removes the only grade decision that changes in a warm metal.

---

### Pick 3 — Textured Ridged Band: $4,590

**Setting:** [Ridged Solitaire in 14K White Gold — $1,100](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-ridged-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147388?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Stone:** [GIA G-VS2 1ct Excellent Cut — $3,490](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28941971?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Total: $4,590**

The ridged solitaire has a textured ridge running along the band. It adds visual mass to the ring without changing the stone or the prong configuration. For men who find a plain grooved band too minimal, the ridge adds detail without crossing into jewelry territory.

The stone is GIA G-VS2 Excellent cut at $3,490. That is the floor for a G-VS2 1ct in certified inventory. VS2 at 1ct is 90%+ eye-clean. The difference between VS2 and VS1 (Pick 1) is $40 on the stone. The difference between grooved and ridged band is $100 on the setting. For $60 more than Pick 1, you get a textured band and similar grade.

**Verdict:** Buy this ring if you want a band with more visual texture than a plain groove. The stone grade is correct. The setting cost is minimal over Pick 1. For more setting comparisons, see [Men's Round Diamond Ring](/mens-round-diamond-ring).

