### Pick 4 — Geometric Statement Frame: $4,640

**Setting:** [Geometric Channel Band in 14K Yellow Gold — $1,410](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/geometric-channel-mens-diamond-wedding-band-in-14k-yellow-gold-650mm-by-james-allen-item-305350?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Stone:** [GIA G-VS2 1ct Excellent Cut — $3,230](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29090690?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Total: $4,640**

This pick uses the lowest-priced GIA 1ct in certified inventory — $3,230 for a G-VS2 Excellent cut. The savings on the stone fund the most distinctive setting in this guide. The geometric channel adds angular frame elements around the band. It looks designed, not standard. The yellow gold here is intentional — it makes the geometric structure visible.

The stone at $3,230 is priced at the floor for a GIA-certified 1ct round. VS2, G color, Excellent cut. No compromise on grade. The price difference from Pick 1's stone ($3,530) is $300 — money you spend on the more expensive setting.

**Verdict:** Buy this ring if design matters more than grade ceiling. You are spending the same total as Picks 1–3 but getting a more distinctive setting and the lowest correct stone.

