### Pick 5 — Platinum with Colorless D Stone: $5,316

**Setting:** [Diagonal Pavé in Platinum — $1,526](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/diagonal-lined-with-pave-diamond-edge-mens-wedding-ring-in-platinum-1-8-ct-tw-item-196082?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Stone:** [GIA D-VS2 1ct Excellent Cut — $3,790](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29255579?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Total: $5,316**

This is the only pick in this guide that uses platinum and D color. D is the highest color grade. It is the only truly colorless grade. Platinum never needs rhodium plating — unlike [white gold](/mens-white-gold-diamond-ring), it stays white forever. In platinum, D color is the correct stone pairing.

The diagonal pavé platinum band has diamond accents set diagonally across the band edge. The band design adds sparkle without looking like a fashion ring. The platinum is 95% pure — it will not fade, it will not need replating.

At $5,316, this is the premium natural pick in this guide. You are paying for two things: the D grade and the platinum setting. The D grade adds about $560 over G at 1ct. The platinum setting adds $526 over white gold. Combined, those decisions add $1,086 over Pick 1. If long-term durability and maximum grade matter, this is the pick.

**Verdict:** Buy this ring if you want the highest grade and the most durable metal in the under-$5,500 budget. Platinum + D color is a correct combination. It will outlast any other setting in this guide.

