### Pick 6 — Wide Pavé Band with Natural 1ct: $5,420

**Setting:** [Pavé Edge in 14K White Gold — $2,180](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/mens-diamond-pave-edge-wedding-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-6-ct-tw-item-196242?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Stone:** [GIA G-VS2 1ct Excellent Cut — $3,240](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29090694?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Total: $5,420**

The pavé edge band has 1/6 ct of diamonds set into the band edges. Small stones, continuous sparkle along the full width. Combined with a 1ct center stone, the total diamond presence on this ring is roughly 1.17ct. This is the highest diamond presence in the natural picks.

The stone is GIA G-VS2 at $3,240. The setting at $2,180 is the most expensive in this guide. That split (40% setting, 60% stone) is unusual — most men's diamond rings spend 70–80% on the stone. This pick reverses the balance. The band carries as much visual weight as the center stone.

Compare this directly to Pick 7. Same setting, $430 more in total — but you get a GIA natural stone that holds commodity value.

**Verdict:** Buy this ring if diamond presence on the band matters as much as the center stone. The setting is worth the premium if you want distributed sparkle across the ring, not just a single point of light.

> "The pavé edge setting is the one setting in men's diamond rings where the band and the center stone talk to each other. The distributed diamonds on the edge balance the center stone visually. Men who want maximum diamond presence without going above $5,500 — this is the setting to look at. The natural 1ct in this band reads larger than a 1ct in a grooved solitaire because the eye moves across the whole ring."
> — Farzana Hasan, diamond expert | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

